PeerJS 1.5.4 — MIT License
==========================

WHY THIS FILE IS HERE. MIT requires that the copyright notice and this permission
notice accompany the software. `peerjs.min.js` sits in this directory and is
distributed by this project, so the notice has to travel with it.

⚠ AN UNRESOLVED PROVENANCE GAP, RECORDED RATHER THAN PAPERED OVER
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

**The vendored file carries no copyright notice, and this project has not invented
one.** Measured over `peerjs-1.5.4/peerjs.min.js`, 92,873 bytes: the string
`copyright` appears zero times, in any case. There is no `@license` banner, no header
comment of any kind — the bundle opens directly with `(()=>{function e(e,t,n,r){`.
`tools/licence-audit.ps1` section A re-measures that zero on every run, so this
paragraph cannot quietly stop being true.

An attribution audit that fabricates an attribution is worse than one that reports a
gap, so the copyright line below is recorded as **UNKNOWN** and `NOTICE.md` records it
as `none-in-vendored-file`. Writing a plausible name and a plausible year here would
have made the audit pass and made it a lie.

WHAT THE FILE DOES CARRY. The bundle embeds its own package metadata, and these are
the only rights-relevant facts that are actually IN the vendored bytes:

    "name":"peerjs"
    "version":"1.5.4"
    "license":"MIT"
    "homepage":"https://peerjs.com"
    "repository":{"type":"git","url":"https://github.com/peers/peerjs"}
    "contributors":["Michelle Bu <michelle@michellebu.com>", …]

So the licence is MIT on the library's own say-so, and a contributors list exists — but
a contributors list is not a copyright line and must not be typed into one.

HOW TO CLOSE THIS. Obtain the `LICENSE` file from the upstream PeerJS 1.5.4 release
artefact, put its exact copyright line in this file and in the `copyright` column of
`assets/lib/NOTICE.md`, and the audit will start checking it the way it checks
Three.js's. Until somebody does that, this gap is printed on every audit run and is
carried as a standing finding in `docs/licensing-audit.md`. It needs network access to
an upstream release, which is precisely the thing this audit is built not to require.

